Definition For a matrix $A \in \mathbb{C}^{n \times n}$, the spectral radius is the largest value $\rho (A) = \max \left| \lambda \right|$ among the moduli of its eigenvalues $\lambda_{1} , \cdots , \lambda_{n}$.
Explanation Generally, the spectrum of a matrix denotes its eigenvalues and eigenvectors collectively; when no matrix is present, the term refers to a corresponding matrix or to eigenvalues and eigenvectors in the abstract linear-algebraic sense1.
See also dominant eigenvalue Gantmacher. (2000). The Theory of Matrices, Vol. 2: p53&#160;&#x21a9;&#xfe0e;

