Overview 1 To adjust the width and height of the figure, you can include the ratio option. Other recommended aliases include aspect_ratios, axis_ratio.
ratio = :none: The default value, where the figure&rsquo;s size is adjusted to fit the ratio. ratio = :equal: Regardless of the figure&rsquo;s size, the x and y axes are adjusted to a one-to-one ratio. ratio = Number: The ratio is adjusted according to Number. Number is given as the ratio in ${{세로} \over {가로}} = {{\Delta y} \over {\Delta x}}$. Code using Plots x = rand(100) y = randn(100) plot(x,y,seriestype = :scatter, ratio = :none) png(&#34;none&#34;) plot(x,y,seriestype = :scatter, ratio = :equal) png(&#34;equal&#34;) plot(x,y,seriestype = :scatter, ratio = 0.5) png(&#34;0.5&#34;) plot(x,y,seriestype = :scatter, ratio = 1) png(&#34;1&#34;) plot(x,y,seriestype = :scatter, ratio = 2) png(&#34;2&#34;) Default :none plot(x,y,seriestype = :scatter, ratio = :none) One-to-One :equal plot(x,y,seriestype = :scatter, ratio = :equal) Specific Ratio Number Number is given as the ratio in ${{세로} \over {가로}}$.
