$$  egin{align*} &amp; Y = X^{2} \ \implies &amp; \sqrt{Y} = X \end{align*} $$ and since $\lambda (X) := X^{2}$ is not a bijective function, the support of $X$ is divided into $x \ge 0$ and $x &lt; 0$. The Jacobian is $dy = 2 x dx$ Therefore, the probability density function of $Y$, $f_{Y}$, will be calculated from $$  egin{align*} f_{Y}(y) =&amp; \sum_{k=1}^{2} {{ \Gamma \left( {{ 
u + 1 } \over { 2 }} ight) } \over { \sqrt{
u \pi} \Gamma \left( {{ 
